WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.435
Tianran: From calorie
counts to portion sizes,

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.104
we wanted to find all the differences

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:07.340
between Domino's in China and in the US.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.009
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:15.415
Here in China, Domino's
comes in three sizes:

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:18.985
the 7-inch small, which is
only available for two pizzas,

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.254
the fruit deluxe and the cocoa brownie,

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.622
hand-tossed only;

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:27.060
the 9-inch regular; and the 12-inch large.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.330
In the US, our Domino's
pizzas come in four sizes:

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.767
small, 10-inch; medium, 12-inch;

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.735
large, 14-inch;

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.972
and the XL, 16 inches.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.874
No, there's nothing on your screen.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.009
The pizza is in fact that greasy.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.048
We have three types of crust,

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:51.284
pan crust, hand-tossed,

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.454
and the thin crust,

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:58.091
and eight different crust
options, including stuffed crusts,

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.493
which are only available
outside of the US.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.462
The UK has them. We have them.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:06.566
Sweet-potato-stuffed crust.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.534
You see that?

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.135
The orangey bit in there.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:12.505
That's pretty good, actually.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.208
It reminds me a little bit of a mooncake

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.243
in that it's sweet and savory.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:22.415
Stuffed sausage crust.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.984
Just a little sausage
peeking out of the hole.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.455
Boletus crust. And
basically it's a mushroom.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.557
It's a variety of mushroom,

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.992
of which there are many different species.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.261
They're actually poisonous,

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.796
so you need to cook them properly.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.866
If they're undercooked, they
will cause hallucinations.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.001
The mushroom seller I met,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:45.105
her husband actually
was poisoned four times,

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.942
and once he saw a bunch of
skulls either side of him.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.344
Once he saw a mountain of gold.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.046
One other time he just beats up a fridge,

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.115
and the last time he slept for three days.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.122
It just tastes like wet mushroom.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.957
Actually, we do have mushrooms

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.558
that make you hallucinate
in the US as well,

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.527
although you can't get them at Domino's.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:11.431
Salted-egg-yolk-stuffed crust.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:15.168
It's recommended that this is
paired with the chicken pizza,

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.871
so you basically have the
whole family in there.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:18.838
That is delicious.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:22.375
It tastes like a million
calories. Such a guilty pleasure.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.409
Mm-hmm.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:26.913
The meat-floss-stuffed crust.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.249
It's not the most appetizing name, is it?

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:32.085
It looks a little bit like lint,

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:35.989
but it tastes like bacon cotton candy.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.891
Usually it's made of pork,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:41.461
but you can also get it as
beef or chicken or fish.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.296
I don't think it quite works in crust

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.598
when crust is already so dry.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.601
We also have something
called the double decker thin

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.004
and the double decker thick.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:51.871
Correct me if I'm wrong.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.375
I think this is actually the
double decadence from the UK.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:03:00.046
I mean, it is pretty
much a pizza sandwich.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:04.817
US Domino's, we have five
different dough varieties.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.620
A better way of saying that is
five different crust options.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.856
Dough varieties, yeah, same thing.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.192
Anyway, first one down here
is a gluten-free crust,

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:14.527
and I want to note that it
only comes in the small,

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.062
because from Domino's perspective,

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.431
if you want gluten-free pizza,
you're eating it by yourself.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:21.234
Next is the hand-tossed, kind
of the classic style, right?

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.402
Everyone's seen the hand-tossed.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.671
To me, it's the default setting.

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:27.674
After that, this is the
crunchy thin, cut into squares.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:30.510
That's a tavern cut, for
all you in the Midwest.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.447
Another crust/dough variety is the pan.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.783
This is a thick boy.
Only comes in a medium.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.519
And, of course, the last
one is the Brooklyn style,

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.688
which you can only get in
the large or the extra large,

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:45.491
and it's thin and also has
these really big slices.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.160
I can't tell. That's eight slices, right?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.228
No, six slices, right?

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.429
So, it should be eight.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:50.930
I don't know. Can someone in post

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.166
increase the contrast on that

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.468
to maybe make the lines
a little more obvious?

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:02.041
Our Domino's largest pizza
has a diameter of 12 inches,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.611
or 30.5 centimeters,

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:06.045
and an area of

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:09.882
730.6 centimeters squared

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:14.721
and costs 88 yuan, or 12.81 USD.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:18.591
Breaking that down, our pizza is 0.11 yuan

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.393
per square centimeter.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:25.031
Take our large 14-inch, or
35.56-centimeter, pizza,

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:29.335
with an area of 993.1 square centimeters.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:32.905
That's 0.15 cents per square centimeter,

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.875
or 0.96 yuan.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.144
That means our US Domino's
pizza per square inch

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:41.447
is roughly 12.5% cheaper than in China.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:47.253
Our Domino's categorizes their
pizzas into three groups,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:50.456
indulgent, classic, and value.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:53.993
Let's take a look at the indulgent first.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:58.298
French-style liver mousse ham pizza.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.733
I'm not even sure what a liver mousse is.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.669
I assume it's meant to be foie gras.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.437
It smells like foie gras.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.177
Oh, but it is weird with pizza, man.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.879
No, that should not be eaten with pizza.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:14.347
That is super weird.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.181
Why?

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.783
Mm, no.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.752
Let's grab some New Zealand lamb.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:25.124
It may be New Zealand lamb,
but they've used a lot of cumin

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.393
and basically turned
it into a lamb skewer.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.962
Definitely miles better after that.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:33.232
The sultan durian pizza.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:37.637
That is a really healthy,
big piece of durian.

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:41.908
Abalone and scallop indulgent pizza.

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:42.975
I mean, just why?

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:46.713
Abalone is super expensive,
and it's popular in China

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:50.216
because its name sounds like
"to get explosively rich,"

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.452
so you'll often find
it served at weddings,

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:53.586
at Chinese New Year.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.624
Ugh.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:05:59.592
Let's clean our palate.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:03.429
We'll get some Australian/New
Zealand wagyu beef.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.233
I'd eat the beef by itself.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.168
I'd remove everything else.

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.938
Crayfish and chicken.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:15.074
I think they've gone full NOLA here,

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:18.010
because the chicken are
meant to be Orlean chicken,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.513
and then we've got them craw daddies, too.

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:21.748
Chicken and crawdads?

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:23.182
I love New Orleans food,

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.984
so yeah, I would
definitely try that pizza.

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:27.920
South American rib eye steak.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.958
The burdock prawn bacon indulgent pizza.

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.559
We've got peas, we've got prawns,

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:35.061
we've got some cherry tomatoes.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.497
This is the Japanese-style-eel pizza,

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:40.833
and on the description, it actually says,

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:44.704
"May contain soft bones. Eat with care."

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:47.807
Oh, they're very tasty, though.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:51.811
Here we have the Australian/South American

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:54.914
grain-fed diced beef, so
they either weren't sure

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:56.649
where the beef was sourced from

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:59.218
or if they run out of beef from Australia,

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.486
they go to South America.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:05.091
And over here we have a
pineapple shrimp pizza.

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:08.094
You know, for those of you
who hate Hawaiian pizzas,

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:10.797
this must be so much more triggering.

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:13.199
No. I think it's actually
worse than a Hawaiian.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:18.070
Also in the indulgent lineup
is our regular durian pizza.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.672
This is actually a best seller.

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:23.009
It costs 9 yuan less than the sultan.

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:25.478
Oh, yeah. No, that's great.

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:28.147
Mm. Oh, that's delicious.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:31.217
Here we have the
okonomiyaki surf and turf.

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.785
Look at that. That's
actually pretty decent.

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:35.822
It's even got the furikake intact.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:39.659
Look at that. These
little superthin flakes.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:40.760
Mm, that's decent.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.995
Well done. Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:44.096
Very meaty, too.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:48.501
Bacon, meat floss, potato pizza,

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:53.372
and it is absolutely
blanketed in meat floss

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:56.175
and a gigantic potato wedge.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:58.644
It's a little bit like the Hawaiian pizza,

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:01.214
except instead of a juicy pineapple

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:05.351
you have sweet
bacon-flavored cotton candy.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.786
Mm, not sure if like.

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:09.489
The Domino's US menu
obviously is not as robust

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:11.657
as China's Domino's menu,

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:13.893
but there are some specialty
pizzas you can get here

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:16.762
that you can't get there, including these.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:21.734
First one here is the
Extravagan, two capital Z's, a.

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:24.237
This looks like a rebranding
of what would be called

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:25.805
a supreme pizza here. Right?

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:28.274
Now, if you hate vegetables, don't worry.

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:31.377
You can get the same pizza
but just MeatZZa version.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:34.847
We got sausage, ham,

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:37.383
pepperoni, possibly hamburger.

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.920
This could have been just a
sausage and pepperoni pizza,

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.055
and it probably would've tasted
the same. I'm just saying.

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:43.890
Philly cheesesteak.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.058
Philadelphia, let us know in the comments

00:08:46.058 --> 00:08:49.395
how insulted you are that the
sandwich that bears your name

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:52.732
is now in pizza form. And
this thing looks terrifying.

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:55.134
Steak, cheese. Like that.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:58.371
Onion and green pepper, oh, and mushrooms.

00:09:00.239 --> 00:09:01.073
Yeah, I mean, it's not bad.

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:02.241
I don't know if I want a
whole thing of this, though.

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:03.509
I already had just one bite,
I'm like, yeah, I got it.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:04.710
It's more the novelty of, yeah,

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.345
I guess that does taste
like a Philly cheesesteak,

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:08.614
but also, now I gotta
eat this whole pizza.

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:09.448
Hm.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.984
A Cali chicken bacon ranch,

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:14.787
which I'm going to go ahead and assume is,

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:15.688
what do you think?

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:18.925
Chicken, bacon, some sort of ranch.

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:20.793
I don't know what makes it California.

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:23.896
That's not bad.

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:24.897
Buffalo chicken.

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:28.100
In China, they had all
these really interesting

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:31.103
flavor combinations that
I'm sure someone was just

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:35.441
really trying to capture the
breadth of Chinese tastes.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:37.209
Here, everything is like,

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:40.179
this exists somewhere else.
We just did a pizza form.

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:41.914
Case in point, Buffalo chicken.

00:09:41.914 --> 00:09:43.115
Hey, do you like wings?

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:43.950
Yeah.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.518
Do you want it in pizza form?

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:46.452
No.

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:48.521
Too bad. Buffalo chicken.

00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:51.057
Another one here, spinach and feta.

00:09:52.058 --> 00:09:52.925
No.

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:56.596
Because I just bit into
a thing of feta cheese.

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:57.430
No.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:59.732
Another specialty pizza we
have exclusive to the US

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:02.401
and not in China is a
Wisconsin six-cheese,

00:10:02.401 --> 00:10:05.204
which, assuming from the name, has,

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:07.273
let me go ahead and guess, six cheeses?

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.341
And they put Wisconsin on there

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:09.942
because Wisconsin is the cheese state.

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:11.077
Shout-out to Wisconsin.

00:10:11.077 --> 00:10:13.980
On to our classic offerings,

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:17.416
beginning with the
salted-egg-yolk-flavored chicken,

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:20.486
which, as you can see, was
very welcomed by the crew.

00:10:20.486 --> 00:10:22.288
We're already missing two pieces.

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:25.558
The Chinese name for this is golden sands,

00:10:25.558 --> 00:10:30.196
which is a specific way of
cooking the salted egg yolk

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:33.899
so that it becomes a sort of frothy paste

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:36.302
that can be used to coat various things.

00:10:36.302 --> 00:10:39.672
It's a salty, sweet umaminess.

00:10:39.672 --> 00:10:42.208
Teriyaki beef potato pizza.

00:10:42.208 --> 00:10:43.776
Teriyaki beef, yes.

00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:46.779
The pizza itself is already quite starchy.

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:49.849
It's all carbs, and then
a potato on top of that.

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:51.384
It's a staple and a staple.

00:10:52.685 --> 00:10:54.754
Most of these pizzas are sweet.

00:10:54.754 --> 00:10:56.522
Peking duck pizza.

00:10:57.456 --> 00:10:58.658
I'm very conflicted about this.

00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:00.426
I like that they're representing us,

00:11:00.426 --> 00:11:05.431
but this looks very blasphemous to me.

00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:06.599
That actually sounds amazing.

00:11:08.367 --> 00:11:10.870
Nope, nope, nope, nope.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:12.304
Blasphemous. No.

00:11:12.304 --> 00:11:13.572
OK, never mind.

00:11:13.572 --> 00:11:14.607
I'd still try it, though.

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:17.843
Here we've got the tuna seafood deluxe.

00:11:17.843 --> 00:11:20.179
Not that big a fan of
seafood pizza, myself.

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:24.517
Truffle-flavored sauce,
mushroom, and chicken pizza.

00:11:24.517 --> 00:11:26.752
Two types of mushrooms in that pizza,

00:11:26.752 --> 00:11:30.423
but note that the truffle
is a flavored sauce,

00:11:30.423 --> 00:11:34.393
so that's not included as one
of the types of mushrooms.

00:11:34.393 --> 00:11:36.595
Ah, no.

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:38.364
Normal pizza, yes.

00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:39.699
Chorizo pizza.

00:11:39.699 --> 00:11:42.601
I don't know why there's
peas on all of the pizza,

00:11:42.601 --> 00:11:46.338
but look, I'm gonna take it
for just regular meat toppings.

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:48.607
Yes, chorizo, get in here!

00:11:50.776 --> 00:11:54.380
Tastes like Bolognese sauce,
but it's OK. I can dig it.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.749
Especially after all of this
stuff, I'll take anything.

00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:59.952
And now our value options,

00:11:59.952 --> 00:12:03.089
beginning with the Texas barbecue.

00:12:03.089 --> 00:12:06.358
Now, the description says it has

00:12:06.358 --> 00:12:08.861
Texas-style meat.

00:12:08.861 --> 00:12:10.963
I assume it's ham.

00:12:10.963 --> 00:12:14.066
Again, it's sweet, but here
since it's a barbecue sauce,

00:12:14.066 --> 00:12:15.668
maybe a honey glaze, I'm OK with that.

00:12:15.668 --> 00:12:17.636
The lychee chicken pizza.

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:19.338
Don't know why it's paired up like that.

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:22.508
This is actually a pretty
meme-errific pizza.

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:25.311
The name is very punny,

00:12:25.311 --> 00:12:30.316
and it references a
middle-aged Chinese influencer

00:12:30.316 --> 00:12:32.952
who screams at the top of his lungs,

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:34.887
"Aoligei!"

00:12:34.887 --> 00:12:38.157
Which kind of just
translates to, "Come on."

00:12:38.157 --> 00:12:40.292
Many times people have said

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:43.162
that I kind of look like
that guy, and it's just,

00:12:43.162 --> 00:12:44.396
I don't know what they're talking about.

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:46.065
There's no resemblance whatsoever.

00:12:46.065 --> 00:12:47.166
Aoligei!

00:12:49.535 --> 00:12:51.103
All I taste is the lychee.

00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:53.005
The potato bacon pizza.

00:12:53.005 --> 00:12:56.776
This is one of Domino's
all-time bestsellers,

00:12:56.776 --> 00:13:00.179
and the name in Chinese
actually says "American style."

00:13:00.179 --> 00:13:03.582
I don't know, is this what
you guys eat over in yonder?

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:05.384
Nope.

00:13:05.384 --> 00:13:06.218
Here we go.

00:13:06.218 --> 00:13:10.723
Here's a taste of America.
Mm-hmm. Land of the free.

00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:13.759
Who am I to judge?

00:13:13.759 --> 00:13:16.228
I don't know what kind of potato wedges

00:13:16.228 --> 00:13:18.430
Americans like to put on their pizza.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.566
Korean-style fried chicken,

00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:24.303
also with sesame seeds, seaweed,

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:27.740
marinara sauce, and
what looks like onions.

00:13:30.209 --> 00:13:32.111
Hey, that's a winner.

00:13:32.111 --> 00:13:33.712
Winner, winner, chicken dinner.

00:13:33.712 --> 00:13:35.815
Veggie deluxe. Not touching it.

00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:37.750
Over here we have something special.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:41.253
These are our two smallest
pizzas, the 7-inchers.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:44.390
This is the fruit deluxe.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:48.661
Peach, blueberry jam,
pineapple, coconut gel.

00:13:50.162 --> 00:13:51.597
Mm!

00:13:51.597 --> 00:13:52.665
You know what's best?

00:13:52.665 --> 00:13:54.166
It's actually meant to be sweet.

00:13:54.166 --> 00:13:55.668
If I've tried one dessert pizza,

00:13:55.668 --> 00:13:56.635
I'm going to try the other one,

00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:59.805
the cocoa-flavored-brownie pizza

00:13:59.805 --> 00:14:03.642
with brownie cubes and cocoa powder.

00:14:03.642 --> 00:14:05.177
It's actually not so bad.

00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:07.913
It reminds me a little bit

00:14:07.913 --> 00:14:11.183
of Nutella on buttered toast.

00:14:11.183 --> 00:14:12.751
I can dig it.

00:14:12.751 --> 00:14:13.752
Still here.

00:14:13.752 --> 00:14:15.421
Man, that's a lot of pizza.

00:14:15.421 --> 00:14:17.523
We at the US Domino's have sandwiches,

00:14:17.523 --> 00:14:19.291
specifically these seven.

00:14:19.291 --> 00:14:23.028
Most of them are just versions of pizza

00:14:23.028 --> 00:14:24.230
that are also in sandwich form,

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.865
first one being the Buffalo chicken.

00:14:25.865 --> 00:14:26.932
Let's get a look in there.

00:14:26.932 --> 00:14:28.834
The chicken, cheese, and the sauce.

00:14:28.834 --> 00:14:30.135
The chicken habanero.

00:14:30.135 --> 00:14:31.136
I like a habanero thing

00:14:31.136 --> 00:14:32.771
because it has the sweet and the spicy,

00:14:32.771 --> 00:14:37.543
pineapple and jalapeños,
together in one bite.

00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:40.279
This one, bleh, Mediterranean veggie.

00:14:40.279 --> 00:14:41.881
Feta cheese and spinach.

00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:43.949
That's in the Mediterranean area, I guess.

00:14:43.949 --> 00:14:47.486
Banana peppers, which I don't
think exist outside of the US.

00:14:47.486 --> 00:14:49.755
Oh, the Philly cheesesteak. Ugh.

00:14:49.755 --> 00:14:51.991
It's double depressing because, I mean,

00:14:51.991 --> 00:14:54.293
the Philly cheesesteak is a sandwich.

00:14:54.293 --> 00:14:55.694
It has a specific way of being made.

00:14:55.694 --> 00:14:57.863
This is not what a Philly cheesesteak

00:14:57.863 --> 00:15:00.266
is supposed to look
like. Why do this? Right?

00:15:00.266 --> 00:15:03.302
Over here we got the chicken bacon ranch.

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:05.404
Bro, they were generous with the ranch.

00:15:05.404 --> 00:15:06.505
Look at that.

00:15:06.505 --> 00:15:09.174
Lots of bacon and chicken and the cheese.

00:15:09.174 --> 00:15:10.209
Nice.

00:15:10.209 --> 00:15:13.379
An Italian sandwich. Mamma mia.

00:15:13.379 --> 00:15:17.249
Salami, cheese, ham, and another salami.

00:15:17.249 --> 00:15:21.387
And, of course, what is more Italian than

00:15:21.387 --> 00:15:23.222
banana peppers?

00:15:23.222 --> 00:15:25.057
And the chicken Parm
sandwich, chicken Parmesan,

00:15:25.057 --> 00:15:29.395
which is, again, an incredibly popular,

00:15:29.395 --> 00:15:31.397
already well-established sandwich

00:15:31.397 --> 00:15:33.032
that Domino's for some reason

00:15:33.032 --> 00:15:35.034
felt they needed to deconstruct

00:15:35.034 --> 00:15:37.169
and then reconstruct in a different way.

00:15:37.169 --> 00:15:39.004
I don't want any of these.

00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:40.439
No sandwiches here in China,

00:15:40.439 --> 00:15:43.442
but what we do have is rib eye steak.

00:15:44.443 --> 00:15:45.644
Waiter!

00:15:53.385 --> 00:15:56.722
Oh, whoa!

00:15:56.722 --> 00:15:58.724
That's a big piece of steak.

00:16:00.492 --> 00:16:01.627
Hm.

00:16:06.298 --> 00:16:08.267
Let's talk pasta and rice.

00:16:08.267 --> 00:16:09.268
We have both!

00:16:09.268 --> 00:16:11.537
Here are our pasta options.

00:16:11.537 --> 00:16:12.938
All come with spaghetti,

00:16:12.938 --> 00:16:17.309
or you can pay one extra
yuan to upgrade to penne.

00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:19.979
Spag Bol. Looks decent. Smells good.

00:16:19.979 --> 00:16:22.247
Lot of Bolognese on the pasta.

00:16:22.247 --> 00:16:24.450
Spaghetti basil.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:27.653
I'm pretty sure that's just a carbonara.

00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:32.358
Here we've got a seafood pasta
with scallop and squid roe.

00:16:32.358 --> 00:16:33.759
Here we've got the rice options.

00:16:33.759 --> 00:16:35.461
Chorizo baked rice.

00:16:35.461 --> 00:16:38.163
You've got some chorizo,
you've got some pepperoni.

00:16:38.163 --> 00:16:41.700
Truffle-flavored baked rice
with chicken and bacon.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.702
Not gonna touch that.
Don't like my truffles.

00:16:43.702 --> 00:16:47.239
And just a nice wholesome curry beef rice.

00:16:47.239 --> 00:16:50.376
Curry sauce, beef, rice.

00:16:50.376 --> 00:16:51.577
What could go wrong?

00:16:51.577 --> 00:16:55.114
No rice dishes in the US, but
we do have our own pastas,

00:16:55.114 --> 00:16:56.382
four specifically.

00:16:56.382 --> 00:17:00.319
This is the fourth Domino's "Food Wars"

00:17:00.319 --> 00:17:01.954
that I have been a part of.

00:17:01.954 --> 00:17:06.859
I want to again state that I
think the pastas at Domino's

00:17:06.859 --> 00:17:09.061
are an absolute abomination.

00:17:09.061 --> 00:17:11.363
So if you're watching from outside the US

00:17:11.363 --> 00:17:14.666
and you think this looks
weird, you are correct.

00:17:14.666 --> 00:17:17.936
This pasta is so weird!

00:17:17.936 --> 00:17:20.539
Italian sausage marinara.

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:22.608
I mean, I can't even break
through the skin of this thing.

00:17:22.608 --> 00:17:23.942
Come on, man.

00:17:23.942 --> 00:17:25.644
Chicken carbonara.

00:17:25.644 --> 00:17:27.212
Ugh.

00:17:27.212 --> 00:17:28.847
Oh, it hurts my soul.

00:17:28.847 --> 00:17:31.316
Ugh! Pasta primavera.

00:17:31.316 --> 00:17:34.520
Whatever primavera means, it ain't this.

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:39.425
And last, chicken Alfredo. Ugh.

00:17:39.425 --> 00:17:40.859
Both countries have wings.

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:44.997
In China, you can only get
your wings in orders of four,

00:17:44.997 --> 00:17:47.900
unless you go for the wings combo.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:51.470
Now, here we have four exclusive flavors.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:53.505
Cantonese roast.

00:17:53.505 --> 00:17:56.775
Sweet in a fruity sort of sweetness,

00:17:56.775 --> 00:17:59.645
and you've got that barbecue smell.

00:18:00.646 --> 00:18:02.548
It tastes like Chinatown.

00:18:02.548 --> 00:18:05.784
Next we have the Orleans flavor.

00:18:05.784 --> 00:18:08.120
Oh, it's very spicy. Wow.

00:18:09.321 --> 00:18:12.624
Oh. Oh, my gosh.

00:18:12.624 --> 00:18:16.361
We also have the honey and
the barbecue-flavored wings,

00:18:16.361 --> 00:18:18.530
and I believe in the US
you just have them combined

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:19.698
as a honey barbecue,

00:18:19.698 --> 00:18:22.468
but here we get an extra flavor out of it.

00:18:22.468 --> 00:18:24.603
I'm sure some of you might have noticed

00:18:24.603 --> 00:18:27.306
our wings look a little bit different.

00:18:27.306 --> 00:18:30.876
A wing is made up of three parts,

00:18:30.876 --> 00:18:34.980
the drum, the flat, and the tip.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:38.150
Usually it's removed because
it doesn't have much meat,

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:40.252
but here in China we love fiddly food.

00:18:40.252 --> 00:18:43.789
Basically, here in China,
we love the tip so much

00:18:43.789 --> 00:18:47.893
that we even have an
entire dish devoted to

00:18:47.893 --> 00:18:49.194
just the tip.

00:18:50.229 --> 00:18:51.763
One thing I do love on the menu, though,

00:18:51.763 --> 00:18:54.066
is the Domino's wings.

00:18:54.066 --> 00:18:58.403
In the US, you can get wing
orders in eight, 16, or 32.

00:18:58.403 --> 00:19:01.073
We only have four exclusive flavors,

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:03.709
starting down here at the hot.

00:19:03.709 --> 00:19:08.013
Then the honey barbecue,
sweet mango habanero,

00:19:08.013 --> 00:19:09.815
and last, the garlic Parmesan.

00:19:09.815 --> 00:19:12.684
On the presentation,
this is especially hm,

00:19:12.684 --> 00:19:13.952
but they are very good.

00:19:13.952 --> 00:19:15.387
I mean, I'd still get pizza over wings,

00:19:15.387 --> 00:19:18.056
but if you're going to get wing sides,

00:19:18.056 --> 00:19:19.825
Domino's wings, not bad.

00:19:19.825 --> 00:19:22.261
We also have roast skewers.

00:19:22.261 --> 00:19:25.430
Now, these are something that
are popular street foods.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:28.934
Here we've got some chicken satay skewers.

00:19:28.934 --> 00:19:30.469
We've got beef skewers.

00:19:30.469 --> 00:19:34.873
These also come in the lamb
version, incredibly delicious,

00:19:34.873 --> 00:19:37.843
and also

00:19:37.843 --> 00:19:39.978
roast sausages.

00:19:39.978 --> 00:19:42.381
I think these are usually
what kids like to eat.

00:19:42.381 --> 00:19:44.616
I don't usually see adults eating these.

00:19:44.616 --> 00:19:48.320
These would be sweet sausages,
but they're very filling.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:52.291
China also has seafood options,
namely our golden shrimp,

00:19:52.291 --> 00:19:54.493
which actually look a little bit orange,

00:19:54.493 --> 00:19:57.930
pollock bites, and regular fish bites.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:01.066
Our other sides include chicken rolls.

00:20:01.066 --> 00:20:05.837
I believe it's smoked chicken,
mayo, and egg and peas.

00:20:05.837 --> 00:20:08.674
Those peas. Peas make it
into every single menu item

00:20:08.674 --> 00:20:09.808
here at Domino's.

00:20:09.808 --> 00:20:13.612
Mini hot dogs wrapped
in a very cute blanket.

00:20:13.612 --> 00:20:16.048
It's almost like it outgrew its blanket.

00:20:16.048 --> 00:20:19.651
Healthy salad, star-shaped hash browns,

00:20:19.651 --> 00:20:23.188
onion rings, and potato wedges.

00:20:23.188 --> 00:20:24.623
Both countries have garlic bread,

00:20:24.623 --> 00:20:26.525
but ours, we do it a little differently.

00:20:26.525 --> 00:20:28.694
Ours is stuffed with
cheese and other stuff.

00:20:28.694 --> 00:20:30.529
For instance, this one right here,

00:20:30.529 --> 00:20:33.999
jalapeño and bacon.

00:20:33.999 --> 00:20:36.568
Why this over pizza?

00:20:36.568 --> 00:20:40.973
Another one we have here
is the spinach and feta.

00:20:40.973 --> 00:20:42.941
We have twists. We have bites.

00:20:42.941 --> 00:20:47.679
Starting over here, we've got
the Parmesan bread twists.

00:20:47.679 --> 00:20:49.748
Looks like it's kind of doing this,

00:20:49.748 --> 00:20:51.917
like please don't give me diarrhea.

00:20:51.917 --> 00:20:54.152
[toilet flushing]

00:20:54.152 --> 00:20:55.387
Garlic bread twists.

00:20:56.788 --> 00:20:58.690
Do you want this taking
up space in your stomach?

00:20:58.690 --> 00:20:59.524
I don't.

00:20:59.524 --> 00:21:00.959
Just get more pizza.

00:21:00.959 --> 00:21:03.061
I mentioned it before. We got dips.

00:21:03.061 --> 00:21:03.895
What are dips?

00:21:03.895 --> 00:21:07.432
From what I can tell, just big portions

00:21:07.432 --> 00:21:09.601
of something to dip these breads in.

00:21:09.601 --> 00:21:12.271
First one is, oh, my good Lord.

00:21:12.271 --> 00:21:14.406
Going to go ahead and assume
this is the five-cheese.

00:21:14.406 --> 00:21:17.643
Look at that, Yuelei.
Look at the oil on this.

00:21:17.643 --> 00:21:18.477
Ugh.

00:21:22.547 --> 00:21:23.448
You know what it tastes like?

00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:26.285
Like pizza, but without the sauce.

00:21:26.285 --> 00:21:28.720
And not to be outdone,
looks like the cheese one,

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:32.190
but this one, you guessed it, has

00:21:34.226 --> 00:21:35.627
marinara sauce.

00:21:35.627 --> 00:21:39.431
So if you got sick of having bread

00:21:39.431 --> 00:21:41.600
with the sauce and cheese on it,

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:43.935
you can just get the
sauce and cheese baked

00:21:43.935 --> 00:21:45.837
and then the bread baked separately

00:21:45.837 --> 00:21:48.206
and just dip them!

00:21:48.206 --> 00:21:49.641
Who wants this instead of pizza?

00:21:49.641 --> 00:21:51.043
I don't understand, but all right.

00:21:51.043 --> 00:21:55.314
We have square garlic
bread and garlic bread.

00:21:55.314 --> 00:21:56.948
I actually don't know
what the difference is

00:21:56.948 --> 00:21:58.216
besides the shape,

00:21:58.216 --> 00:22:01.520
but they both come with
this honey mayo dip.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:03.955
I actually thought this was mustard.

00:22:06.058 --> 00:22:08.293
I think it's mustard, mayo, and honey.

00:22:08.293 --> 00:22:10.762
I think the bread is just
an excuse to eat this dip,

00:22:10.762 --> 00:22:12.364
because it is actually pretty good.

00:22:12.364 --> 00:22:14.666
We also have soups.

00:22:14.666 --> 00:22:19.204
You can get a nice bowl
of pumpkin cream bacon,

00:22:19.204 --> 00:22:23.709
classic borscht, or
cream of mushroom soup.

00:22:23.709 --> 00:22:24.609
Desserts.

00:22:24.609 --> 00:22:27.646
Unfortunately, both China
and the US have lava cakes,

00:22:27.646 --> 00:22:29.047
so it is not exclusive,

00:22:29.047 --> 00:22:31.183
but we have a couple things
that you can't get in China,

00:22:31.183 --> 00:22:34.986
specifically these cinnamon bread twists

00:22:34.986 --> 00:22:38.590
and the Domino's marbled cookie brownie.

00:22:38.590 --> 00:22:40.359
Come on, who doesn't like brownies?

00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:42.761
And you can tell they put a
little cookie dough in there.

00:22:42.761 --> 00:22:44.763
It's a cookie-brownie hybrid.

00:22:44.763 --> 00:22:48.200
And we got this icing that
you would dip in here,

00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:49.735
and I'm not going to do it.

00:22:49.735 --> 00:22:53.672
I've decided I'm taking a stand
against all twisted bread.

00:22:53.672 --> 00:22:55.407
Not happening, sorry.

00:22:55.407 --> 00:22:58.844
Here in China, our
exclusive dessert options

00:22:58.844 --> 00:23:02.614
are limited to durian pie.

00:23:02.614 --> 00:23:03.749
I believe this is durian.

00:23:03.749 --> 00:23:05.083
I had a sniff.

00:23:05.083 --> 00:23:06.852
It's durian.

00:23:06.852 --> 00:23:08.420
You can always tell if
something is durian.

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:09.621
Just put your nose to it.

00:23:09.621 --> 00:23:11.390
Pineapple pie,

00:23:11.390 --> 00:23:15.527
and we have one of two

00:23:15.527 --> 00:23:17.796
Portuguese egg tarts.

00:23:17.796 --> 00:23:22.300
Drinks. In the US, you can
get Sprite, Fanta orange,

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:25.637
Dasani water, and Dr Pepper.

00:23:25.637 --> 00:23:30.008
This is emblic leafflower

00:23:30.008 --> 00:23:32.778
and coconut jelly.

00:23:32.778 --> 00:23:34.679
I had to do quite a bit of research

00:23:34.679 --> 00:23:36.748
to figure out what an emblic is.

00:23:36.748 --> 00:23:39.418
Apparently it's some kind of fruit

00:23:39.418 --> 00:23:41.787
that actually has a lot
to do with Buddhism,

00:23:41.787 --> 00:23:45.157
but it has great cooling

00:23:45.157 --> 00:23:47.092
and cough-relieving properties,

00:23:47.092 --> 00:23:50.462
so this is perfect for summer
when it's too hot outside.

00:23:52.431 --> 00:23:53.265
Oh.

00:23:55.133 --> 00:23:56.968
It's kind of nice, but
it also kind of tastes

00:23:56.968 --> 00:24:00.338
like I'm drinking green
perfume, if that makes sense.

00:24:00.338 --> 00:24:02.441
It's very, very floral.

00:24:02.441 --> 00:24:06.678
This is coconut and musk melon.

00:24:06.678 --> 00:24:08.146
Hm.

00:24:08.146 --> 00:24:09.080
Oh, that's tasty.

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:13.018
It's a little bit too
rich, so nay to that.

00:24:13.018 --> 00:24:14.519
And this,

00:24:14.519 --> 00:24:18.657
this is carambola and olive.

00:24:18.657 --> 00:24:20.559
It's such a weird combination, right?

00:24:20.559 --> 00:24:22.894
So, a carambola is this thing.

00:24:24.029 --> 00:24:27.599
It's a star fruit, but I've
never had it as a drink.

00:24:27.599 --> 00:24:31.937
And together with Chinese olive? OK.

00:24:31.937 --> 00:24:33.572
Learn something new every day.

00:24:35.507 --> 00:24:38.376
Mm. Oh, that was a pleasant surprise.

00:24:38.376 --> 00:24:40.645
There was actually some coconut
jelly at the bottom, too,

00:24:40.645 --> 00:24:41.847
that was very inviting.

00:24:41.847 --> 00:24:46.084
We also just have a regular
mango and passion fruit drink.

00:24:46.084 --> 00:24:49.654
Oh, and bottled water.

00:24:52.891 --> 00:24:56.094
Domino's entered China in 1997,

00:24:56.094 --> 00:24:59.397
but for about two decades, they
pretty much just floundered

00:24:59.397 --> 00:25:01.733
and nobody really took notice of them.

00:25:01.733 --> 00:25:03.502
It was only really in recent years

00:25:03.502 --> 00:25:06.238
that they've become very youthful

00:25:06.238 --> 00:25:10.275
with all sorts of wacky
flavors, as you've seen,

00:25:10.275 --> 00:25:12.811
and because it's not
as common as McDonald's

00:25:12.811 --> 00:25:17.182
or KFC in China, a Domino's
opening in, for example,

00:25:17.182 --> 00:25:21.286
a tier-two, tier-three
city is big news to locals,

00:25:21.286 --> 00:25:24.155
and a lot of people actually
post about it on social media.

00:25:24.155 --> 00:25:26.324
"Oh, look, a Domino's
has come to our town."

00:25:26.324 --> 00:25:28.026
It's something to be proud of.

00:25:28.026 --> 00:25:29.027
Domino's in the US,

00:25:29.027 --> 00:25:32.197
I feel like it's been
Domino's versus Pizza Hut,

00:25:32.197 --> 00:25:34.833
Pizza Hut versus Domino's
since I think the '80s.

00:25:34.833 --> 00:25:37.269
Yes, there's other
nationwide pizza chains.

00:25:37.269 --> 00:25:39.070
Papa Johns sucked up
a lot of the attention

00:25:39.070 --> 00:25:40.305
online for a while.

00:25:40.305 --> 00:25:41.806
There's Little Caesars,
there's a bunch of other ones,

00:25:41.806 --> 00:25:44.075
but it really is Domino's and Pizza Hut

00:25:44.075 --> 00:25:44.876
have been neck and neck.

00:25:44.876 --> 00:25:46.978
I mean, they're kind of interchangeable.

00:25:46.978 --> 00:25:48.246
Now people watching are
going to be like, "No,

00:25:48.246 --> 00:25:50.181
one's better than the other."

00:25:50.181 --> 00:25:51.783
Honestly, I don't think I
could taste the difference

00:25:51.783 --> 00:25:54.653
if you put them side by
side, but with Domino's,

00:25:54.653 --> 00:25:56.254
as far as the reputation, you always know

00:25:56.254 --> 00:25:58.523
you're going to get a
good pizza, a hot pizza,

00:25:58.523 --> 00:26:01.426
it's going to be decently
priced, which is nice.

00:26:01.426 --> 00:26:04.829
Here in China, Domino's
main rivals are, of course,

00:26:04.829 --> 00:26:07.165
Pizza Hut, who dominates the market

00:26:07.165 --> 00:26:10.035
with a steady 5% market share.

00:26:10.035 --> 00:26:13.672
Next in line is a local
brand called Champion Pizza,

00:26:13.672 --> 00:26:16.675
with 5.6% of the market share.

00:26:16.675 --> 00:26:18.677
And third comes Domino's,

00:26:18.677 --> 00:26:21.947
at 5.3% of the market share.

00:26:21.947 --> 00:26:26.618
Like in the States, Domino's
China has a guarantee

00:26:26.618 --> 00:26:29.187
to deliver your pizza within 30 minutes.

00:26:29.187 --> 00:26:31.856
Otherwise, they will give
you all sorts of discounts.

00:26:31.856 --> 00:26:33.925
This really sets them apart

00:26:33.925 --> 00:26:35.694
from other pizza players here in China,

00:26:35.694 --> 00:26:38.396
because they use their own
proprietary delivery service,

00:26:38.396 --> 00:26:42.100
whereas most restaurants
in China use a third party

00:26:42.100 --> 00:26:44.636
akin to something like Uber Eats.

00:26:44.636 --> 00:26:46.237
It's also something that's become

00:26:46.237 --> 00:26:49.007
a bit of a double-edged
sword, because people

00:26:49.007 --> 00:26:52.877
will actively try and game
their 30-minute delivery window

00:26:52.877 --> 00:26:57.248
by switching off corridor
lights, removing door numbers,

00:26:57.248 --> 00:26:58.817
and just generally trying to get

00:26:58.817 --> 00:27:00.752
their delivery drivers lost,

00:27:00.752 --> 00:27:04.956
and about half of all of Domino's

00:27:04.956 --> 00:27:07.993
salary payments go towards
their delivery drivers,

00:27:07.993 --> 00:27:11.162
which shows you how big of
a delivery force they have,

00:27:11.162 --> 00:27:13.064
which is actually kind of quite nice.

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:14.599
Convenience, I mean, Domino's is probably

00:27:14.599 --> 00:27:16.768
one of the most convenient pizza chains

00:27:16.768 --> 00:27:18.003
in the United States.

00:27:18.003 --> 00:27:20.338
You can get a Domino's pizza,
you can get it in the app,

00:27:20.338 --> 00:27:22.240
it's easy to use, the
pizza's at your place

00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:24.576
in probably 30 minutes,
depending where you live.

00:27:24.576 --> 00:27:26.277
Some would say too convenient.

00:27:28.813 --> 00:27:30.715
The Domino's in China doesn't disclose

00:27:30.715 --> 00:27:32.250
their nutritional information,

00:27:32.250 --> 00:27:35.453
but based on third-party
independent research,

00:27:35.453 --> 00:27:40.025
we found that a large
hand-tossed pepperoni pizza

00:27:40.025 --> 00:27:44.496
has 1,466.4 calories,

00:27:44.496 --> 00:27:46.631
64 grams of protein,

00:27:46.631 --> 00:27:49.701
66.4 grams of fat,

00:27:49.701 --> 00:27:53.238
155.2 grams of carbs,

00:27:53.238 --> 00:27:57.542
and 3,257.6 milligrams

00:27:57.542 --> 00:27:58.677
of sodium.

00:27:58.677 --> 00:28:01.946
Our large pepperoni is
370 calories per slice,

00:28:01.946 --> 00:28:05.784
or 2,960 for the entire pie.

00:28:05.784 --> 00:28:10.188
Also, 299% of your daily sodium.

00:28:10.188 --> 00:28:13.892
Oy! That's a salty pie.

00:28:13.892 --> 00:28:18.663
Domino's China's most
calorific pizza is this,

00:28:18.663 --> 00:28:22.734
the large salted-egg-yolk-flavored
chicken pizza

00:28:22.734 --> 00:28:25.203
with stuffed sausage crust.

00:28:25.203 --> 00:28:28.139
Now, one slice is 230 calories,

00:28:28.139 --> 00:28:33.111
and the full pizza is 1,841 calories.

00:28:33.111 --> 00:28:34.846
Our Domino's pizza with the most calories

00:28:34.846 --> 00:28:37.716
is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

00:28:37.716 --> 00:28:40.919
An extra-large slice is 560 calories,

00:28:40.919 --> 00:28:44.923
and the full pie, 3,360 calories.

00:28:47.559 --> 00:28:50.428
Two ingredients you won't
find in Domino's in China

00:28:50.428 --> 00:28:53.832
are potassium bromate and ractopamine.

00:28:53.832 --> 00:28:56.367
Both have been banned for use in China.

00:28:56.367 --> 00:28:58.570
Potassium bromate is used
as a dough conditioner,

00:28:58.570 --> 00:29:01.706
and it's classified as
a category 2B carcinogen

00:29:01.706 --> 00:29:04.275
by the International Agency
for Research on Cancer.

00:29:04.275 --> 00:29:06.611
Ractopamine is FDA-approved,

00:29:06.611 --> 00:29:08.613
and it promotes muscle-mass development,

00:29:08.613 --> 00:29:12.150
limits fat deposition, and
reduces feed consumption.

00:29:12.150 --> 00:29:14.652
Although it is considered
safe for human consumption,

00:29:14.652 --> 00:29:17.956
China requires all meats
sold to be free of the drug

00:29:17.956 --> 00:29:20.358
and never fed the product to begin with.

00:29:20.358 --> 00:29:22.927
There is no direct link
stating ractopamine

00:29:22.927 --> 00:29:25.463
is specifically used in
the meat at Domino's,

00:29:25.463 --> 00:29:28.166
but on their stewardship
page under "Animal Care,"

00:29:28.166 --> 00:29:30.769
they state, quote, "It's
important to highlight

00:29:30.769 --> 00:29:33.538
that Domino's does not
own, raise, transport

00:29:33.538 --> 00:29:36.808
or process the animals
used for our products.

00:29:36.808 --> 00:29:39.711
Domino's purchases pork,
beef and poultry ingredients

00:29:39.711 --> 00:29:42.213
from suppliers who obtain their products

00:29:42.213 --> 00:29:44.549
from farmers and ranchers
who raise and care

00:29:44.549 --> 00:29:46.818
for their animals in
compliance with local,

00:29:46.818 --> 00:29:50.288
state and federal guidelines,
industry best practices

00:29:50.288 --> 00:29:53.224
and the support of farm
and animal veterinarians."

00:29:53.224 --> 00:29:57.028
That is a very long legalese
way of Domino's saying,

00:29:57.028 --> 00:29:59.397
"Hey, we don't farm the meat.

00:29:59.397 --> 00:30:01.166
We buy them from other people,

00:30:01.166 --> 00:30:02.433
and they're saying they're
doing it the right way,

00:30:02.433 --> 00:30:04.669
so we don't know."

00:30:04.669 --> 00:30:06.838
I was traumatized as a kid

00:30:06.838 --> 00:30:10.542
because I had a fish bone
stuck horizontally in my throat

00:30:10.542 --> 00:30:11.810
and I had to go to the hospital,

00:30:11.810 --> 00:30:14.445
and the doctor basically reached
in and just yanked it out,

00:30:14.445 --> 00:30:17.482
and for many years I just
did not want to eat fish,

00:30:17.482 --> 00:30:20.718
but in China, it's fish with
bones or nothing at all,

00:30:20.718 --> 00:30:21.586
so tough luck.

00:30:21.586 --> 00:30:23.354
You just gotta suck it up.

